+# Star road-edge checkpoint tolerance — 2026-10-07
+
+Owner follow-up: steep Star curves still miss checkpoints while the car remains mostly on the road. Requirements **G01 / R01 / T01–T04 / V03–V05 / Q01 / SP09**. SP09 covers the complete local paved/kerb cross-section and shallow edge recovery without crediting skipped corners.
+
+The remaining failure is reproduced and fixed. A smooth line 5.5 m from the centreline stays entirely on real road/kerb cells but fails rules19 at gate9. Its crossing is 16.781 m along the corner plane, beyond that gate's 15.637 m acceptance span. Merely adding spline corner gates in the previous repair did not cover this part of the actual road sweep.
+
+## Behavior and bounds
+
+Gate configuration measures the connected road/kerb cross-section, stopping at the first gap. The scan is locally bounded by the authored road width: ordinary gates scan up to half-width +1.5 m; corner gates up to the greater of that bound and 1.5 times their miter half-span. This covers the spline sweep beyond its chord-derived estimate without jumping across grass to a returning road branch. The road span uses the midpoint of the final 0.25 m raster interval. Acceptance adds a **1 m recovery margin** on either side, including steep curves; the existing separate gentle-turn and outside recovery allowances remain.
+
+Star keeps **all 19 mandatory ordered gates**. Gate centres, directions, ordering, layer checks, finish line and return-to-missed-section behavior are retained. The marker uses the actual new asymmetric span. No automatic +5 s penalty, progress-based gate credit, checkpoint deletion or map widening is added. Canonical car handling and physical road geometry are untouched by this task.
+
+The scoring contract advances explicitly to **standing-5-road-gates-v20**. Existing immutable v12–v19 revisions derive the new effective contract for metadata/tickets; new board hashes remain separate from historical boards. Rivalry eligibility recognizes those old revisions under an active v20 verifier. No stored track or score migration is performed. The concurrent physics0.53 work is preserved; the independent full replay below verifies against that current physics contract, compiler22 and pinned engine.
+
+## Source and exact verification
+
+The retained exact original Star fixture is `game/tests/fixtures/star_spline_lap.json`. The current public Star cached by the separate discovery diagnostic has identical pieces, start line, route points/widths, objects, paint, layout and name; comparison hashes are retained. The original draft/WIP paths used on October 6 are no longer present, so no current original-file checksum claim is made. This task never writes player saves, public track content or live services.
+
+Actual commands use `scripts/dev.ps1` and pinned Godot **4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf**:
+
+- `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1 TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_star_gate_tolerance.gd`: **156 checks, zero failures**. Eighteen paths cover both start-line directions and centre/edge offsets through ±6 m, each completing five laps. Through ±5.5 m every 0.2 m sample is paved/kerb; ±6 m paths are checked throughout to remain within 1 m of actual paved/kerb cells. The exact task-start v19 implementation still fails the identical entirely paved −5.5 m line at gate9. Twelve deeper infield cuts reject, all recover by returning through the required gates, and no automatic penalties accrue. All 19 marker spans and their outer acceptance bounds are checked.
+- The real compact edge-guided drive uses a separate route only to choose quantized controls. Every physical/scored step uses the unchanged original Star map. **Five laps / 46,138 ticks / zero collisions**, followed by exact state/lap replay. Full inputs are retained in `star-edge-five-lap-replay.json`.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe docs/evidence/star-gate-tolerance-2026-10-07/verify_edge_replay.py`: real local **GodotVerifier accepts all five laps**, ticks **46,138**, lap ticks `[9303, 9203, 9217, 9205, 9210]`, rules20 / physics0.53. No ticket, score submission or online service is used.
+- Existing tests via the same `TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/<file>` entry: `test_checkpoint_rules.gd` **266**, `test_checkpoint_notices.gd` **533**, `test_checkpoint_bridge_layers.gd` **259**, `test_bridge_entry_checkpoints.gd` **258**, `test_bridge_exit_checkpoints.gd` **2527**, `test_rewind.gd` **57**, `test_app.gd` **99**, all zero failures. The original Star regression now passes **51** checks, including its five centreline/physical laps, real centre/inside driving and original v18 failure. Its shortcut fixture now measures actual excursion depth: shallow recovery is expressly permitted by this owner request, while the six deeper cuts still reject. Test recordings now go to `build/star-spline-laps`, preserving the historical October 6 proofs.
+- `... TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_script_parse.gd`: **332 scripts, zero failures**.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest backend/tests/test_verifier.py backend/tests/test_review_reliability.py backend/tests/test_rivalry.py backend/tests/test_track_lifecycle.py -q -k 'not postgres' -x`: **130 passed / 1 skipped / 60 deselected**, **122.06 s**, one existing Starlette deprecation warning. Disposable local databases only; PostgreSQL cases were excluded. Historical contact replay/timing and immutable-manifest preservation checks remain.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe -m ruff check backend/bmt_backend/contracts.py backend/bmt_backend/rivalry.py backend/tests/test_verifier.py backend/tests/test_review_reliability.py`: **all checks passed**. Scoped `git diff --check`: exit0, existing CRLF normalization notices only.
+- `.tools/backend-venv/Scripts/python.exe docs/evidence/star-gate-tolerance-2026-10-07/create_checkpoint.py`: **18 task-only source/document files**. `git apply --reverse --check docs/evidence/star-gate-tolerance-2026-10-07/scoped-change.patch`: exit **0**. Actual task-start snapshots are retained separately; the review baseline excludes concurrent physics0.53/shared-file edits and status entries. Git index untouched.
+- `... TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_star_gate_tolerance.gd -Graphical`: **5 checks, zero failures**, actual native before/after configured gates on the same map/camera/vehicle pose. Both images inspected. These are paused diagnostic marker views, not fabricated race results.
+
+Initial edge regression: **3 failures**, at offsets −6, −5.5 and +6 m. The first widened-span test had four shortcut assertions fail across the two directions: those two chord paths touched only three/five grass samples and remain within 1 m of pavement. The regression now explicitly distinguishes the newly authorized shallow recovery from deeper infield shortcuts; it retains 12 deep-cut rejection/recovery checks. The first sandboxed engine run could not create its standard user log; approved runs used the pinned engine's normal logs. Initial diagnostic camera placement did not clearly show the rejected endpoint; the final captures are centred on the actual missed paved crossing. No full Validate, Android export/install, phone attachment check or physical-device test was performed.
+
+## Files, review and acceptance
+
+Runtime: `game/race/track_session.gd`, `race_rules.gd`; backend `contracts.py`, `rivalry.py`. Test contracts: `test_checkpoint_rules.gd`, `test_bridge_exit_checkpoints.gd`, `test_star_spline_laps.gd`; new `test_star_gate_tolerance.gd`, `capture_star_gate_tolerance.gd` and their UIDs; `backend/tests/test_verifier.py`, `test_review_reliability.py`, `fixtures/verified_oval.json`; `scripts/dev.ps1` includes the new regression in Validate. This task changes the oval's expected rules key only; concurrent physics updates are excluded from its scoped checkpoint. Documentation: this report and both project status files.
+
+[Before](evidence/star-gate-tolerance-2026-10-07/before-first-corner.png) / [after](evidence/star-gate-tolerance-2026-10-07/after-first-corner.png), complete replay, local verification receipt, source comparison, task-start snapshots and command logs are retained under `docs/evidence/star-gate-tolerance-2026-10-07/`. The review patch preserves concurrent edits and leaves the Git index untouched.
+
+Restart the race in the updated local build; no Star edit/republication is required. **Online use requires a matching rules20 API/verifier rollout**; this task performs no live backend/cloud/NAS deployment, publication or board rewrite. Existing tickets must retain their matching rules workers during rollout. Owner driving acceptance and physical-device testing remain.
